    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0626" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/104</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Siam</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-31T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>American International Corporation has proposed to Siamese Government, through
                    Pitkin, purchase nine recently seized German steamers. Inform Siamese
                    Government, corporation trusts its proposal will be favorably received. You are
                    instructed to take such steps as you may find possible to expedite the
                    transaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
